From Arabic into Iberia and beyond
In al-Andalus, the Arabic word {{translit|ar|(al-)bāḏinjān}} was borrowed into the Romance languages in forms beginning with b- or, with the definite article included, alb-:
 Portuguese {{lang|pt|bringella}}, {{lang|pt|bringiela}}, {{lang|pt|beringela}}
 Spanish {{lang|es|berenjena}}, {{lang|es|alberenjena}}

The eggplant is quite often featured in the older scientific literature under the junior synonyms S. ovigerum and S. trongum. Several other names that are now invalid have been uniquely applied to it:
 Melongena ovata {{small|Mill.}}
 Solanum album {{small|Noronha}}
 Solanum insanum {{small|L.}}
 Solanum longum {{small|Roxb.}}
 Solanum melanocarpum {{small|Dunal}}
 Solanum melongenum {{small|St.-Lag.}}
 Solanum oviferum {{small|Salisb.}}
 Prachi {{small|Salisb.}}

 Uso culinário 
{{mais fontes|Esta secção|ciência=sim|data=dezembro de 2009}}
Pode ser usada no preparo de pratos como o cuscuz, o suflê, a mussaca, torta, salada, recheada, entre outras várias formas na cozinha. Também é muito boa para fazer lasanha.

